# Symbols of the win-x86 image (Learn & Play): NAME ADDRESS CONVENTION PROTOTYPE (tools/targets/targets.py).
# ADDRESS: runtime address at the image base 0xf80000 (what F_<addr> and the vtables hold; link address +
# 0xb80000). CONVENTION: cdecl, stdcall, thiscall, fastcall, custom (a function; custom = register arguments
# whole-program optimisation (LTCG) made up, the comment says which registers), data (a global), code (an
# address inside a function). PROTOTYPE: the Mac's, as far as it is known (- = not recorded); the
# convention, not the prototype, says how the arguments arrive.
# Matched against the Mac image by class_info / QueryInterface pairs, library call order, exports, unique
# strings, name tables and vtable shape; a `# medium` or `# low confidence` comment marks the weaker matches.
# MSVC folds QueryInterface and QueryInterface_const, so both names share one address (two names may).
# `NAME unsupported REASON` = no counterpart in this image, or not matched yet. One name per line, grouped
# by the list in names/ that has it first.

